Description of parameter relationships:
FEATCADM-rfSharingEnabled:
If rfSharingEnabled is set to 'true', at least one instance of SMOD_EXT must be configured;
SMOD-distRefPoint: distRefPoint may be set only, if prodCodePlanned refers to FSMF or FSMFA or FSIH system module;
if prodCodePlanned refers to FSMF or FSMFA or FSIH system module and external fault line 13 is used (parameter inUse under EAC_IN with portId equal to 13 set to true) then description of this line (parameter desc) must be set to "Mains power break";
if prodCodePlanned refers to FSMF or FSMFA or FSIH system module and external fault line 14 is used (parameter inUse under EAC_IN with portId equal to 14 set to true) then description of this line (parameter desc) must be set to "Power module failure";
if prodCodePlanned refers to a FSMF or FSMFA or FSIH system module then parameter portId must be smaller than 27;

If SBTS is planned in AirScale+FSMF configuration and
a) there's no CABLINK between AirScale BBMOD and FSMF (SMOD or their BBMODs) with firstEndpointLabel equal to OPT, the radio modules configured with LTE or 5G RAT have to be connected to AirScale BBMODs (WCDMA and GSM RAT can be configured on same radio module only if there is a second link from that radio module towards FSMF or its FBBx for WCDMA or GSM RAT IQ data routing). The radio modules configured with WCDMA or GSM RAT have to be connected to FSMF or its FBBx (LTE or 5G RAT can be configured on same radio module only if there is a second link from that radio module towards AirScale for LTE or 5G RAT IQ data routing).
b) there is CABLINK between AirScale BBMOD and FSMF (SMOD or their BBMODs) with firstEndpointLabel equal to OPT configured, the radio modules configured with LTE or 5G RAT cannot be connected to FSMF SMOD or its BBMODs.

To find out on which radio module the cell is configured, check MNL/MNLENT/CELLMAPPING/(LCELC/LCELW/LCELL/LCELNR)/CHANNELGROUP/CHANNEL/antlDN which includes RMOD ID in the path.
To find out where this RMOD is connected, check all CABLINKs where firstEndPointDN or secondEndPointDN is this RMOD.

If MNL.productVariantPlanned is set to sBTS and SMOD.prodCodePlanned refers to ASIK system module, then GSM/WCDMA/LTE RAT cannot be configured (GNBTS/WNBTS/LNBTS MOCs cannot be defined).

